# What `railway up` uploads. The Dockerfile copies only python/ and
# data/queue-payload-*.json, so everything else is upload time spent on files
# the image discards -- 60MB of repo for a build that needs about 1MB.
#
# Every path here is anchored with a leading slash, and has to be: these are
# gitignore-style patterns, so a bare `scripts` matches at any depth and would
# take `python/scripts/` with it -- which is the whole server.
/node_modules
/artifacts
/.git
/docs
/src
/scripts

# Every data file except the payload the server actually serves. The board and
# ADP CSVs are gitignored anyway; the drafts and demo pages are megabytes of
# things the queue builder never reads.
/data/*
!/data/queue-payload-*.json
